<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="AprilinParis-C-Theme" spTempo="142">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1932
Composer:	Vernon Duke
Lyricist:	E. Y. “Yip” Harburg
Form:	32-bar AABA
Style:	Swing
Key:	C major

It was written for the Broadway revue 
Walk a Little Faster. The tune is often performed
instrumentally, especially in the famous Count Basie
arrangement, but the original song had lyrics by
Harburg. Its opening section contains some
sophisticated harmonic movement and key changes,
even though the tune is generally listed in C major.</spComments>
